      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Exactly what I was running into in my UdonGraph video player setup. The Sample UdonSyncPlayer (Unity) prefab uses \"player\" as the variable name for the BaseVRCVideoPlayer component. My player variable was randomly getting set to Null after running PlayURL.\nThat this bug is present in the sample prefabs is setting a lot of people up for failure (myself included).",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-05-30T04:15:43.277Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "RunEvent in UdonBehaviour.cs will clear the wrong program variables on a behaviour when receiving an event that takes arguments. This can be a problem when the arguments names are something common like \"player\"\nRunEvent currently sets some parameters with slightly mangled names to use as the arguments for events that take arguments such as OnPlayerJoined(VRCPlayerApi player). The problem is that it has some code from before the name mangling was automatic which gets called after the event fires and clears the parameters, but uses the wrong name for them. \nThe code in question is \n```\nforeach ((string symbolName, object _) in programVariables)\n{\n    SetProgramVariable(symbolName, null);\n}\n```\nWhich can just be removed from UdonBehaviour.cs as an easy fix. The problem is that this code uses the unmangled name for the parameter. So after something like OnPlayerLeft(VRCPlayerApi player) is called, instead of clearing the parameter variable `onPlayerLeftPlayer`, the variable named `player` is cleared which will confusingly break any Udon program that defines a variable named `player`.",
  "error": null,
  "eta": null,
  "etaPublic": true,
